<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bergen auf Rügen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergen">Bergen</a> auf Rügen is the main inland town of the island of Rügen in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecklenburg-vorpommern">Mecklenburg-Vorpommern</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Its Church of St Mary was begun in the late 12th century by Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaromar-i-of-rugen">Jaromar I of Rügen</a> and given in 1193 to a convent of Cistercian nuns, around which the town grew. It long served as the administrative centre of the island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bergen-auf-rugen.jpg" alt="Bergen auf Rügen" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagar66 based on work of TUBS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bergen_auf_R%C3%BCgen_in_VR.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
